### MetroMiles API - manual test requests
### Works in Visual Studio 2022 (17.8+, built-in) and VS Code (REST Client extension).
### Run top to bottom - each request reads ids straight out of the previous response, no manual
### copy/pasting of Guids required.
### Note: response-chaining expressions ({{requestName.response.body...}}) are written inline at
### the point of use, not assigned to a standalone @variable — some .http editors (Visual Studio's
### built-in one included) evaluate @variable assignments eagerly for the whole file, which fails
### before the referenced request has ever run. Inline references are evaluated lazily instead.
### Every endpoint returns the same enveloped shape: {"resultData": {...}, "isSuccessful": true, ...}
### - so every chained reference below goes through ".resultData.".

@baseUrl = https://localhost:44366
@contentType = application/json

### 1) Login with the admin user seeded by IdentitySeeder.cs
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/Login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@metromiles.com",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### 2) Create a Brand
# @name createBrand
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Brands
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "name": "Toyota",
  "description": "Japanese automobile manufacturer"
}

### 3) Create a Fuel
# @name createFuel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Fuels
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "name": "Gasoline"
}

### 4) Create a Transmission
# @name createTransmission
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Transmissions
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "name": "Automatic"
}

### 5) Create a Model (brandId/fuelId/transmissionId pulled straight from steps 2-4)
# @name createModel
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Models
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "brandId": "{{createBrand.response.body.$.resultData.id}}",
  "fuelId": "{{createFuel.response.body.$.resultData.id}}",
  "transmissionId": "{{createTransmission.response.body.$.resultData.id}}",
  "name": "Corolla",
  "dailyPrice": 1200.50,
  "imageUrl": "https://example.com/images/corolla.jpg"
}

### 6) Create a Car (modelId pulled straight from step 5)
# Status: 1 = Available, 2 = Rented, 3 = UnderMaintenance
# @name createCar
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Cars
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "modelId": "{{createModel.response.body.$.resultData.id}}",
  "kilometer": 0,
  "mile": 0,
  "modelYear": 2026,
  "plate": "34ABC123",
  "minFindexScore": 700,
  "status": 1
}

### 7) Create another user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Users
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Doe",
  "email": "jane.doe@metromiles.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### --- Read/list endpoints ---

### Get Brands
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Brands
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Get Fuels
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Fuels
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Get Transmissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Transmissions
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Get Models (paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Models?PageIndex=0&PageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Get Cars (paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Cars?PageIndex=0&PageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Get Users (paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Users?PageIndex=0&PageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### --- Auth token lifecycle ---

### Refresh rotates (revokes) the token it's given and returns a brand new one - resending the SAME
### token a second time correctly fails with 401 ("already revoked"). To refresh again, chain off
### the previous refresh's own response, not off login's original token - see the second request below.

### Refresh token (1st hop - uses the refreshToken captured at login)
# @name refresh1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/RefreshToken
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "token": "{{login.response.body.$.resultData.refreshToken}}"
}

### Refresh token again (2nd hop - uses the NEW refreshToken from the 1st hop, proving rotation chains correctly)



POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/RefreshToken
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "token": "{{refresh1.response.body.$.resultData.refreshToken}}"
}

### Revoke token (uses login's original refreshToken - only works if neither Refresh request above was run first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/RevokeToken
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "token": "{{login.response.body.$.resultData.refreshToken}}"
}

### Change password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/ChangePassword
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "currentPassword": "Admin123!",
  "newPassword": "Admin123!New"
}

### --- Sessions ---

### Get full session history (paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/Sessions?PageIndex=0&PageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Get only active sessions (paged)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/Sessions/Active?PageIndex=0&PageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Revoke a specific session by id (replace with an id from one of the two lists above)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Auths/Sessions/PASTE_SESSION_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### --- Roles ---

### List roles (with their permission claims)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Roles
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

### Create a role
# @name createRole
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Roles
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "name": "BrandManager"
}

### Add a permission claim to the role (roleId pulled straight from the create above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/Roles/{{createRole.response.body.$.resultData.id}}/claims
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.resultData.token}}

{
  "claimValue": "brands.delete"
}

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
